From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 04:57:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: Disable features a firmware build advertises
 but lacks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Apple's BCM4355 firmware answers the "p2p" iovar, so brcmfmac enables
P2P, but it fails "p2p_da_override" with -52 and every P2P device
creation fails at startup:

  brcmf_p2p_set_firmware: failed to update device address ret -52
  brcmf_p2p_create_p2pdev: set p2p_disc error
  brcmf_cfg80211_add_iface: add iface p2p-dev-wld0 type 10 failed: err=-52

Add a table of features to disable per firmware ID, next to the
existing override table, and list the iPad 5 and iPad 6 builds. Apple
uses AWDL rather than Wi-Fi P2P.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from OrchardLinux/hardware#6 0002 (J71t ledger 4.6), the
 feature.c part only, moved ahead of the iPad 5 as the J71b RAM test
 notes ask; adds the J71b FWID 01-d0cb7703 (iPadOS 17.7.11).]
Signed-off-by: Dalton Alexandre <alley.nightly_0b@icloud.com>
---
 .../broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/feature.c     | 31 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/feature.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/feature.c
index 488364ef8..3e140019f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/feature.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/feature.c
@@ -104,6 +104,36 @@ static const struct brcmf_feat_fwfeat brcmf_feat_fwfeat_map[] = {
 	{ "01-d2cbb8fd", BIT(BRCMF_FEAT_MONITOR_FMT_HW_RX_HDR) },
 };
 
+/* Features a given firmware build advertises but can't actually do */
+static const struct brcmf_feat_fwfeat brcmf_feat_fwfeat_disable_map[] = {
+	/*
+	 * Apple BCM4355 firmware answers the "p2p" iovar but fails
+	 * "p2p_da_override" with -52, so every P2P device creation fails.
+	 * Apple uses AWDL, not Wi-Fi P2P.
+	 */
+	/* iOS 16 C0 "FearA" (iPad 5), 9.44.205.0.3.50.46 */
+	{ "01-9787ef4d", BIT(BRCMF_FEAT_P2P) },
+	/* iPadOS 17.7 C1 (iPad 6), 9.30.503.2.3.50.99 */
+	{ "01-d0cb7703", BIT(BRCMF_FEAT_P2P) },
+};
+
+static void brcmf_feat_firmware_disables(struct brcmf_pub *drv)
+{
+	const struct brcmf_feat_fwfeat *e;
+	int i, j;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(brcmf_feat_fwfeat_disable_map); i++) {
+		e = &brcmf_feat_fwfeat_disable_map[i];
+		if (strcmp(e->fwid, drv->fwver))
+			continue;
+		for (j = 0; j < BRCMF_FEAT_LAST; j++)
+			if (e->feat_flags & drv->feat_flags & BIT(j))
+				brcmf_info("firmware %s: disabling feature %s\n",
+					   e->fwid, brcmf_feat_names[j]);
+		drv->feat_flags &= ~e->feat_flags;
+	}
+}
+
 static void brcmf_feat_firmware_overrides(struct brcmf_pub *drv)
 {
 	const struct brcmf_feat_fwfeat *e;
@@ -343,6 +373,7 @@ void brcmf_feat_attach(struct brcmf_pub *drvr)
 
 	brcmf_feat_wlc_version_overrides(drvr);
 	brcmf_feat_firmware_overrides(drvr);
+	brcmf_feat_firmware_disables(drvr);
 
 	brcmf_fwvid_feat_attach(ifp);
 
-- 
